      "overviewText": "This **7 Days Kerala Tour Package with Kovalam** is a well-balanced holiday designed for families and couples looking to experience Kerala’s hills, wildlife, backwaters, and beaches in one smooth journey. The itinerary combines relaxed travel, scenic sightseeing, and comfortable private stays, making it ideal for a first-time Kerala visit.\n\nThe trip begins in **Kochi** and takes you to the misty hill station of **Munnar**, known for tea gardens and cool weather. From there, you head to **Thekkady** for nature and wildlife experiences, followed by a peaceful **Alleppey houseboat stay** through Kerala’s iconic backwaters. The journey ends at **Kovalam**, offering laid-back beach time and a visit to **Thiruvananthapuram**.\n\nWith private vehicle transfers, handpicked hotels, and multiple stay categories—from **Basic to Luxury**—this Kerala package focuses on comfort, flexibility, and hassle-free travel.\n\n\n### Places Covered in This Kerala Tour Package\n### \n#### **Munnar**\n#### \nMunnar is one of the most popular hill stations in Kerala, known for its vast **tea plantations**, mist-covered hills, waterfalls, and pleasant climate. It is a key highlight in most Kerala tour packages and ideal for nature lovers, families, and couples looking for scenic beauty and relaxed sightseeing.\n\n#### **Thekkady**\n#### \nThekkady is famous for the **Periyar Wildlife Sanctuary** and lush spice plantations. This destination offers a mix of forest landscapes, wildlife experiences, and cultural activities, making it an essential stop in a Kerala itinerary focused on nature and eco-tourism.\n\n#### **Alleppey**\n#### \nAlleppey, also known as Alappuzha, is the hub of Kerala’s iconic **backwaters**. An overnight **houseboat stay in Alleppey** is one of the most searched and recommended experiences in Kerala tour packages, offering peaceful cruising through canals, villages, and coconut-lined waterways.\n\n#### **Kovalam**\n#### \nKovalam is a well-known **beach destination in Kerala**, popular for its crescent-shaped beaches, lighthouse views, and calm coastal atmosphere. It is ideal for beach relaxation and adds a leisure element to a Kerala family or honeymoon tour package.\n\n#### **Thiruvananthapuram**\n#### \nThiruvananthapuram (Trivandrum), the capital of Kerala, is known for its cultural landmarks, temples, museums, and city attractions. It is commonly included in Kerala tour packages combined with Kovalam for sightseeing and local experiences.\n\n\n### Why You Should Opt for This Kerala Tour Package\n### \n- **Complete Kerala Experience:** Hills, wildlife, backwaters, and beaches in one itinerary\n- **Private Tour:** Dedicated vehicle and driver for comfort and flexibility\n- **Alleppey Houseboat Stay Included:** One of Kerala’s most iconic experiences\n- **Multiple Hotel Categories:** Choose from Basic, Standard, Premium, or Luxury\n- **Family-Friendly Itinerary:** Relaxed pace with minimal long travel days\n- **Great Value for Money:** Starting at ₹30,800 with major inclusions covered\n\n### Important Tips for Kerala Trip\n### \n- **Best Time to Visit:** October to March for pleasant weather\n- **Pack Light Cotton Clothes:** Kerala has a warm and humid climate\n- **Carry Comfortable Footwear:** For sightseeing and short walks\n- **Book Premium/Luxury Stays Early:** Especially during peak season\n- **Respect Local Culture:** Dress modestly at temples and religious sites",
