      "overviewText": "The **Kerala Holiday Package (6 Days / 5 Nights)** is designed for travelers who want a relaxed yet complete Kerala experience without rushing. Covering hill stations, wildlife, backwaters, and a cultural city, this itinerary is ideal for families, couples, and first-time visitors to Kerala.\n\nYour journey starts from **Kochi** and takes you to the scenic hills of **Munnar**, followed by a nature-focused stay in **Thekkady**. The highlight of the trip is a peaceful **Alleppey houseboat stay** through Kerala’s backwaters, before returning to Kochi for local sightseeing and departure.\n\nWith a **private taxi**, multiple hotel categories (Basic to Luxury), and a comfortable pace, this Kerala holiday package focuses on convenience, value for money, and a stress-free travel experience.\n\n\n### Places Covered in This Kerala Holiday Package\n### \n#### **Munnar – Hill Station & Tea Gardens (2 Nights)**\n#### \nMunnar is one of the most popular hill stations in Kerala and a key highlight of this Kerala holiday package. Known for its vast tea plantations, misty hills, waterfalls, and pleasant climate, Munnar offers relaxed sightseeing and scenic views, making it ideal for families, couples, and first-time Kerala travelers.\n\n#### **Thekkady – Wildlife & Spice Plantations (1 Night)**\n#### \nThekkady is famous for the **Periyar Wildlife Sanctuary**, spice plantations, and forest landscapes. This destination adds a nature and eco-tourism experience to the Kerala itinerary, with opportunities for boating, plantation visits, and peaceful stays surrounded by greenery.\n\n#### **Alleppey – Backwaters & Houseboat Stay (1 Night)**\n#### \nAlleppey (Alappuzha) is the heart of Kerala’s backwaters and one of the most searched destinations in Kerala tour packages. An overnight **Alleppey houseboat stay** lets you cruise through palm-lined canals, village life, and serene waterways, making it the highlight of this Kerala holiday package.\n\n\n#### **Kochi – Culture & Heritage (1 Night)**\n#### \nKochi (Cochin) is a historic coastal city known for Fort Kochi, Chinese fishing nets, colonial architecture, and cultural landmarks. The Cochin sightseeing day adds a cultural and urban touch to the Kerala holiday itinerary before departure.\n\n\n### Why You Should Opt for This Kerala Holiday Package\n### \n- **Balanced Kerala Itinerary:** Hills, wildlife, backwaters, and city life in one trip\n- **Alleppey Houseboat Included:** A must-do Kerala backwaters experience\n- **Private Tour Comfort:** Dedicated vehicle and driver-cum-guide\n- **Multiple Stay Categories:** Choose from Basic, Standard, Premium, or Luxury\n- **Family-Friendly Pace:** Comfortable travel days, suitable for all age groups\n- **Great Value Package:** Starting at ₹23,800 with key inclusions covered\n\n\n### Important Tips for Kerala Holiday Trip\n### \n- **Best Time to Visit:** October to March for pleasant weather\n- **Pack Light Cotton Clothing:** Kerala weather is warm and humid\n- **Carry Comfortable Footwear:** Useful for sightseeing and short walks\n- **Book Early During Peak Season:** Especially for Premium and Luxury stays\n- **Respect Local Culture:** Dress modestly at temples and cultural sites",
